ef=\"#font_9_68\" transform=\"matrix(10.5,0,0,-10.5,175.47644,21.536225)\" fill=\"#18283a\"/>\n<use xlink:href=\"#font_9_86\" transform=\"matrix(10.5,0,0,-10.5,182.56394,21.536225)\" fill=\"#18283a\"/>\n<use xlink:href=\"#font_9_87\" transform=\"matrix(10.5,0,0,-10.5,188.81143,21.536225)\" fill=\"#18283a\"/>\n<use xlink:href=\"#font_9_3\" transform=\"matrix(10.5,0,0,-10.5,193.83042,21.536225)\" fill=\"#18283a\"/>\n<use xlink:href=\"#font_9_80\" transform=\"matrix(10.5,0,0,-10.5,197.48444,21.536225)\" fill=\"#18283a\"/>\n<use xlink:href=\"#font_9_72\" transform=\"matrix(10.5,0,0,-10.5,208.42545,21.536225)\" fill=\"#18283a\"/>\n<use xlink:href=\"#font_9_72\" transform=\"matrix(10.5,0,0,-10.5,215.54444,21.536225)\" fill=\"#18283a\"/>\n<use xlink:href=\"#font_9_87\" transform=\"matrix(10.5,0,0,-10.5,222.66345,21.536225)\" fill=\"#18283a\"/>\n</g>\n</svg>\n","1 → 2 → 3 → 2 ...; slow and fast meet"],["heading","JAVA EXAMPLE"],["code","class Node { Node next; }\nstatic boolean hasCycle(Node head){\n    Node slow=head,fast=head;\n    while(fast!=null && fast.next!=null){\n        slow=slow.next;fast=fast.next.next;\n        if(slow==fast)return true;\n    }\n    return false;\n}"],["heading","OUTPUT AND ANALYSIS"],["text","For 1→2→3→2 returns true. O(n) time, O(1) space."],["heading","INTERVIEW QUESTION"],["heading","Why use two pointers instead of a set?"],["text","It detects linked-list cycles with constant extra space."],["heading","PRACTICE YOURSELF"],["text","What is the result for a single node pointing to itself?"]]